\ A read of a binding whose value is not proven to read back as one push. The input is untyped, and
\ its callers pass both a number and a quotation, so nothing narrows it to a number either. A
\ quotation would be called on read with an effect nothing states, so the build refuses the word
\ rather than compile a read that might diverge from the interpreter.

pass-through: ( a -- a ) [
  kept: swap ;
  kept
] ;

7 pass-through .
[ 8 ] pass-through .
